{"agent":"main","body":{"error":null,"exit":0,"for_seq":15,"result_bytes":563,"result_hash":"sha256:d2bace78cb0a6dba26a15c9c687689fe239b82f3c142f68f17bd39d635d476b3","result_inline":"1\t# slugify changelog\n2\t\n3\t## 2.0.0\n4\t\n5\tBreaking:\n6\t- `slugify(text, separator)` is now `slugify(text, options)`. Passing a string as the second argument is no longer supported.\n7\t- Lowercasing is opt-in: pass `{ lower: true }`. 1.x always lowercased.\n8\t- The default separator is `_` (was `-`).\n9\t\n10\tAdded:\n11\t- `strict: true` drops every character that is not a letter or a digit instead of turning runs of them into a separator.\n12\t\n13\t## 1.4.2\n14\t\n15\t- Combining marks are stripped after NFKD normalisation, so accented letters become their base letter.\n16\t","served":"live","truncated":false,"wall_ms":0},"hash":"sha256:207548e9d54a49272de16d60a9aa1f47f38e484e1fa1fd1c0ac60684fd0c4d67","mono_ns":16000000,"prev":"sha256:37f990ea615ea49a387396bdf76044caa91fcba0ef3d22d66f81d5f6ff63c281","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":16,"session":"c06eca7c-52a2-4ae8-8d1f-d968a2dc0055","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.016Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_result"}
