{"agent":"main","body":{"args_hash":"sha256:de832a9a95b48af559f2c597cf98e583adef94584b3e53e008811eaa43b2a03a","args_inline":{"content":"---\nname: vendor-slugify-api\ndescription: vendor/slugify was bumped to 2.0.0 with a breaking API change (options object, opt-in lowercase, default separator \"_\")\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`vendor/slugify/index.ts` was bumped to 2.0.0. Breaking changes vs 1.x (see `vendor/slugify/CHANGELOG.md`):\n- `slugify(text, separator)` string second arg no longer supported — must pass `slugify(text, { separator, lower, strict })`.\n- Lowercasing is opt-in via `{ lower: true }` (1.x always lowercased).\n- Default separator changed from `-` to `_`.\n\n**Why:** `src/pages.ts` still called `slugify(title, \"-\")` using the old signature, so the string was treated as a truthy-but-property-less options object — separator fell back to `_`, producing underscored slugs in new pages and breaking `test/pages.test.ts`.\n\n**How to apply:** If slugs or other vendor-derived output look wrong after a vendor bump, check `vendor/*/CHANGELOG.md` for breaking API changes before assuming the bug is in `src/`. Fixed by calling `slugify(title, { separator: \"-\", lower: true })`.\n","file_path":"/private/var/folders/yb/b_617z_s2ml933nmr_k7m47m0000gn/T/saga-bench-1958376525/ts-0015-slugify-api-drift/1/cfg/claude-config/projects/-private-var-folders-yb-b-617z-s2ml933nmr-k7m47m0000gn-T-saga-bench-1958376525-ts-0015-slugify-api-drift-1-ws/memory/vendor_slugify_api.md"},"component":"harness","cwd_rel":".","index_version":null,"tool":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_012omrjq3oTM3BtJixHYB9kk"},"hash":"sha256:fba95f4d826132a9c23436b1e610d88be17bb0acbfb590635676feaf096fff76","mono_ns":21000000,"prev":"sha256:5a14093563b01999a46726702fd577cf13bee9324ce20e9cfafd867cbf04600c","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":21,"session":"c06eca7c-52a2-4ae8-8d1f-d968a2dc0055","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.021Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_call"}
